  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1105 AM MST Mon Nov 16 2026\n\nHigh pressure will continue to be situated over the area today \nallowing for clearing skies and winds becoming calmer, following \nbreezy winds in the morning from the backdoor cold front that pushed \nthrough the region earlier. Highs will be in the low to mid 60s \ntoday.\n\nOn Tuesday an upper level trough will shift through the region. \nThis will allow for southwesterly winds to feed some moisture into\nour midlevels. Soundings support moisture in the mid levels as \nwell. This will bring a low chance for light precipitation in the\nevening for areas of higher elevation areas of western New \nMexico. This upper trough will also bring breezy conditions \nTuesday afternoon across the area with speeds generally 10-20 mph.\n\n\nFollowing the passage of the storm system on Wednesday high pressure \nwill build back into the area which will bring a brief period of \ncalmer weather. Another upper level trough will move into the area \nFriday. This will bring the potential for breezy winds, with gusts \nbetween 30-40 mph and brings in cooler air for the weekend.",
